  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset: one 4:3 landscape painting for The Burnt Book Sanskrit learning story. Request 1536 x 1152 native output or the closest supported native 4:3 resolution. Refined Indian watercolor with restrained gouache on warm ivory paper; organic detail, quiet ochre, sage, dusty terracotta, muted indigo. Warm, gentle, evocative storytelling, consistent character design.\nCanonical scene brief: The burning-ground grove at night: the Vetāla seated on a root rubbing his hands; a tiny round spirit of old paper in round spectacles with scrolls under both arms and one finger wagging at the sky; Dādī and Śuka beside you; a faint image in the smoke of a king and a hungry beggar on a lane.\nCharacter appearances:\nyou: Always seen from behind or at a distance, face never detailed, so every learner can be the hero: a young person in a simple ochre kurta with a cloth shoulder bag.\ndadi: A warm, sharp-eyed grandmother in her seventies, silver hair in a low bun, round spectacles, a cream cotton sari with a thin maroon border and a grey shawl; carries a cloth-bound notebook.\nshuka: A bright green rose-ringed parrot with a red beak and a faint pink and black neck ring, a little scruffy, very expressive eyes; usually on your shoulder or Dādī's.\nvetala: A long, thin, ash-grey spirit hanging upside down from a śiṃśapā branch by its ankles, arms folded across its chest, bright amused eyes, a shawl of mist trailing downwards; strange, never frightening.\nvidhika: A small round spirit of old paper with tiny round spectacles and rolled palm-leaf scrolls under both arms, one finger always wagging.\nPhone-first composition: clear compact narrative grouping, essential faces, hands and objects comfortably inside all edges. Show the complete scene without border. No collage or multi-panel layout.\nWriting is permitted by the owner. This particular scene needs no readable inscription; focus on its narrative. Do not invent scripts or fill small objects with pseudo-lettering. No watermark or UI. All human and humanoid figures wear complete opaque traditional clothing or robes.",
